1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,103
What if the stars traced your movements?

2
00:00:03,143 --> 00:00:04,767
You walk home at night,

3
00:00:04,807 --> 00:00:06,214
and with every step,

4
00:00:06,254 --> 00:00:08,456
a new star blinks on above you,

5
00:00:08,496 --> 00:00:11,639
connected to the last by a thin golden line.

6
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:15,111
Soon the whole town is looking up.

7
00:00:15,151 --> 00:00:17,441
The sky is covered in glowing paths.

8
00:00:17,481 --> 00:00:19,901
Bakers' loops, mail carriers' zigzags,

9
00:00:19,941 --> 00:00:23,267
and one very tangled spot that belongs to a toddler.

10
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:25,539
You try to hide.

11
00:00:25,579 --> 00:00:27,302
You duck into a basement,

12
00:00:27,342 --> 00:00:30,054
and your star hovers over the roof like

13
00:00:30,094 --> 00:00:31,324
a patient firefly.

14
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:33,581
The sky can't see through walls,

15
00:00:33,621 --> 00:00:35,839
but it remembers where you went.

16
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,828
Lying doesn't work either.

17
00:00:38,868 --> 00:00:40,413
I stayed home all night,

18
00:00:40,453 --> 00:00:41,800
you tell your friend,

19
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,641
while the sky quietly draws three ice cream

20
00:00:44,681 --> 00:00:45,632
cones in a row.

21
00:00:45,672 --> 00:00:48,539
Your friend raises one very patient eyebrow.

22
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:51,255
Astronomers get excited.

23
00:00:51,295 --> 00:00:53,843
Constellations are no longer ancient myths.

24
00:00:53,883 --> 00:00:55,829
Orion is just a man who walks his

25
00:00:55,869 --> 00:00:56,913
dog every evening.

26
00:00:56,953 --> 00:00:58,538
In this thought experiment,

27
00:00:58,578 --> 00:01:00,524
the sky becomes a gigantic diary.

28
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,804
At night, a child asks a question:

29
00:01:03,844 --> 00:01:04,974
who is watching us?

30
00:01:05,014 --> 00:01:07,067
An old telescope shows the answer.

31
00:01:07,107 --> 00:01:07,498
Nobody.

32
00:01:07,538 --> 00:01:09,099
The stars aren't watching.

33
00:01:09,139 --> 00:01:11,254
They're simply keeping you company,

34
00:01:11,294 --> 00:01:12,424
like quiet friends.

35
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:14,704
Here's the twist.

36
00:01:14,744 --> 00:01:16,056
When the child walks,

37
00:01:16,096 --> 00:01:17,408
the stars drift down,

38
00:01:17,448 --> 00:01:20,433
one by one, to hover beside her like fireflies.

39
00:01:20,473 --> 00:01:22,300
They aren't tracing her path.

40
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:24,681
They've just been following her home.

41
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:28,427
So tonight, when you walk under the sky,

42
00:01:28,467 --> 00:01:30,440
don't worry about being watched.

43
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,635
Wave at your stars.

44
00:01:31,675 --> 00:01:34,844
Somewhere above, a thousand tiny lights are happily

45
00:01:34,884 --> 00:01:38,053
drawing your whole life as one long, shining heart.
